Advanced Bayesian Quantitative Framework for Financial Forecasting & Microstructure Execution 

Overview : 

This repository implements a hybrid Bayesian State-Space & Stochastic Volatility (SV) Framework designed to model complex, heteroscedastic, 
and time-varying dynamics in high-frequency/daily financial price series (specifically EUR/USD).By synthesizing Hamiltonian Monte Carlo (HMC) inference via Stan,
Non-Linear State Transitions (UKF / GRU / LSTM), and an Institutional Smart Money Concepts (SMC) & Price Action decision layer, this project bridges the gap 
between macroeconomic stochastic modeling and order-flow microstructure execution.

Key Architectural Features: Bayesian Stochastic Volatility & Latent State Dynamics Markov-Switching Regimes (HMM).

      Alternates between trending and choppy/scalping market regimes, dynamically modulating momentum persistence, liquidity 
      sensitivity, and mean-reversion parameters.Non-Linear OU Restoration Force: Implements a state-dependent Ornstein-Uhlenbeck (OU) mean-reversion process that 
      pulls price toward an adaptive EMA attractor during range-bound regimes, while remaining inactive during structural trends.Hybrid Volatility Component:

      Combines HAR-type volatility structures, GJR-GARCH innovations, macroeconomic news event dynamics, and jump-diffusion mechanisms to model heteroscedasticity 
      and tail risk.Deep Sequential Memory: Injects non-linear temporal memory using Quasi-Momentum LSTM and Bidirectional GRU architectures into the state-transition
      function.

Tiered Decision Layer (SMC & Microstructure Signal Hierarchy)Rather than relying purely on unconstrained statistical forecasts, predictive 
t-Student distributions are mapped into a tiered, rule-governed signal hierarchy:

Tier 1 (Deterministic Priority Triggers): 

    High-conviction institutional events—such as Liquidity Sweeps, Multi-Touch Big Figure Exhaustion Counts (3 tests), and Order Block Mitigations with 
    Volume Displacement—override baseline forecasts to enforce sharp directional entries.

Tier 2 (Continuous Logit Integration): 

   In the absence of Tier 1 triggers, the model falls back to a continuous decision layer that blends Order-Flow proxy metrics (CVD & RSI Confluences) 
  with a quantitative Price Action Scoring System (Fair Value Gaps, Structural Breakers, Doji Geometries).[ MCMC / HMC Posterior Sampling ]
